-- title:
--   Theorem 1, p. 11 — under Assumptions 1–2 and inf f > −∞, the DASGD iterates satisfy E[‖∇f(X_n)‖²₂] → 0
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $d \ge 0$, $X=\mathbb R^d$ with the Euclidean norm $\|\cdot\|_2$; the random function $F(x;\xi)$ lives on a probability space $(\Xi,\mu)$ and $f(x)=\mathbb E_\mu[F(x;\xi)]$; the noise sequence $(\omega_n)_{n\ge0}$ lives on a second probability space $(\Omega,\mathbb P)$, is i.i.d. with law $\mu$, and $X_n$ are the DASGD iterates $X_0=x_0$, $X_{n+1}=X_n-\alpha_{n+1}\nabla F(X_{s(n)},\omega_{n+1})$ with a deterministic delay schedule $s(n)\le n$. Assumption 1 is taken with a bound $B\ge\sup_x\mathbb E\|\nabla F(x;\xi)\|_2^2$ and a Lipschitz constant $L$ of $x\mapsto\mathbb E[\nabla F(x;\xi)]$. Let $X_n$ be the DASGD iterates generated by Algorithm 3. Under Assumptions 1 and 2, if $\inf_{x\in\mathbb R^d}f(x)>-\infty$, then $f$ is differentiable, each $\|\nabla f(X_n)\|_2^2$ is integrable, and
--
--   $$\lim_{n\to\infty}\mathbb E\big[\|\nabla f(X_n)\|_2^2\big]=0.$$
--
--   Assumption 2 is the disjunction of four delay regimes, so the theorem covers bounded delays, delays growing like $n^p$ ($p<1$), linearly growing delays and delays growing like any polynomial $n^q$, each with its own step-size law. For a general nonconvex smooth objective, the gradient of the asynchronous SGD iterates vanishes in mean square.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The conjuncts "$f$ is differentiable" (Remark 1) and "each $\|\nabla f(X_n)\|_2^2$ is integrable" (presupposed by the expectation in (5)) are part of the paper's claim, made explicit because Lean's `gradient` is $0$ at non-differentiable points and the integral of a non-integrable function is $0$. "$\inf f>-\infty$" is `BddBelow (Set.range f)`.
-- source:
--   Z. Zhou, P. Mertikopoulos, N. Bambos, P. W. Glynn, Y. Ye, Distributed Stochastic Optimization with Large Delays, arXiv:2107.02919v1, p. 11, Theorem 1, eq. (5)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_LargeDelaySGD_MeanSquare_Model

namespace LargeDelaySGD.MeanSquare

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory

theorem theorem_1 {d : ℕ} {Ξ Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ξ] [MeasurableSpace Ω]
    (μ : Measure Ξ) [IsProbabilityMeasure μ] (P : Measure Ω) [IsProbabilityMeasure P]
    (F : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin d) → Ξ → ℝ) (B : ℝ) (L : NNReal) (hA1 : Assumption1 F μ B L)
    (α : ℕ → ℝ) (s : ℕ → ℕ) (hA2 : Assumption2 α s)
    (hinf : BddBelow (Set.range (objective F μ)))
    (ω : ℕ → Ω → Ξ) (hω : IIDNoise P μ ω) (x₀ : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin d))
    (X : ℕ → Ω → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin d)) (hX : IsDASGD F α s ω x₀ X) :
    Differentiable ℝ (objective F μ) ∧
      (∀ n, Integrable (fun a => ‖gradient (objective F μ) (X n a)‖ ^ 2) P) ∧
      Filter.Tendsto (fun n => ∫ a, ‖gradient (objective F μ) (X n a)‖ ^ 2 ∂P)
        Filter.atTop (nhds 0) := by sorry

end LargeDelaySGD.MeanSquare
